                  <h2>How to Make a Cashless Claim</h2>
                  <ol>
                    <li>Confirm that the hospital is in your insurer’s network and speak to the hospital’s insurance or TPA desk.</li>
                    <li>Submit the pre-authorization form with the doctor’s treatment plan, diagnosis and cost estimate.</li>
                    <li>Share supporting reports, such as the biopsy, histopathology and PET-CT reports.</li>
                    <li>Wait for approval; IRDAI’s 2024 rules require insurers to decide on cashless requests within one hour and on final discharge authorization within three hours.</li>
                    <li>Request an enhancement if treatment changes or the hospital stay is extended.</li>
                    <li>At discharge, pay only for non-payable items and any deductions.</li>
                  </ol>
                  <p>For reimbursement claims, keep the discharge summary, all original bills, pharmacy receipts, investigation reports and payment receipts, and submit them within the time limit stated in your policy.</p>
